{
  "_about": "Reviewed seed mapping legacy AX free-text industry strings onto industry facet slugs. This is deliberately NOT a complete table. Measured against state/ax_case_harvest_registry.json at implementation time: 231 cases carry 173 DISTINCT free-text values ('grocery delivery / e-commerce', 'superapp (mobility, delivery, fintech)', ...). A complete one-to-one table is not achievable, and pretending otherwise would invite guessing.",
  "config_version": 1,
  "map_version": 1,

  "_normalization": "Lookup key = the original string with Unicode NFKC applied, whitespace runs collapsed to one space, ends stripped, then casefold(). NOTHING else. The normalization must not itself be a guess: no synonym folding, no punctuation removal, no token reordering. The record always keeps the EXACT original in provenance.raw.",

  "_unmapped_policy": "A non-empty legacy value with no entry here becomes reporting state 'unmapped_legacy_value': an unresolved[] entry carrying the exact term, the exact original preserved in provenance.raw, NO slug guessed, and the legacy value NEVER presented as classification evidence. It is counted separately and never folded into 'unresolved'. Migration is never blocked on it: the 231 AX cases land in cases/case-studies, where case_facets is schema-optional and coverage is report-only in v1.",

  "_admission_rule": "An entry belongs here only when the string alone unambiguously identifies the ADOPTING organisation's industry. Hybrids, platforms, marketplaces and super-apps are deliberately left out: 'superapp (mobility, delivery, fintech)' and 'e-commerce / fintech' name several industries and the string cannot say which one the deployment served. Leaving them unmapped is the honest outcome, not a gap to be closed by judgement.",

  "_evidence_rule": "A mapped value yields facet_evidence with field 'legacy_field' and the exact original as matched_term. An UNMAPPED value yields no evidence at all — it is a reviewer to-do, not a fact about the case.",

